======================================================================================================================
PART 1 -- TASK 1: THE REQUIRED LIFETIME WINDOW.
======================================================================================================================

  The two edges, stated as hypotheses before any number is computed.
    LOWER EDGE (must still be there for the third peak).  The third peak's height is set by the cold density AT
    recombination; Planck measures omega_c = 0.1200 +/- 0.0012, a 1.0% (1 sigma) box.  Requiring the decayed
    fraction at z_* to sit inside 1 sigma gives  1 - exp(-t_*/tau) <= 0.0100  =>  tau >= t_*/0.010050.
    UPPER EDGE (must be gone where rotation curves are measured).  L61's branch-independent 'excess spent once'
    theorem: a theory whose kernel already reproduces the RAR with the cold component switched off OVERSHOOTS
    pointwise by the transmitted pull eta*g_halo.  L49/L50 put the ceiling at eta <= 0.582 (canonical a0 =
    9.3619e-11) / 0.486 (alt a0 = 1.1279e-10) for a kernel reading the baryons only (eps=0), and 0.355 / 0.276
    if it reads the total potential (eps=1); at eta = 1 the median SPARC overshoot is 1.692x (+0.228 dex).  The
    SURVIVING FRACTION plays exactly the role of eta.  'Gone by' is a CHOICE, so all four choices are reported.

  LOWER EDGE:  t_* = 3.7175e+05 yr;  allowed decayed fraction at z_* = 0.0100  =>  tau >= 0.036989 Gyr = 36.99 Myr
  [PASS] W1  the LOWER edge is a real finite constraint: surviving recombination to Planck's 1% box on omega_c requires tau >= 35-40 Myr
           (tau_lo = 0.036989 Gyr = 36.99 Myr)

  UPPER EDGE  tau <= t_gone / ln(1/eta_max):
    definition of gone-by                              t [Gyr]   canon eps=0     alt eps=0   canon eps=1     alt eps=1
    z=0   rotation curves are measured today           13.7971       25.4895       19.1215       13.3223       10.7174
    z=2   z~2 disc kinematics exist                     3.2706        6.0424        4.5328        3.1581        2.5406
    z=5   a halo here leaves a dynamical imprint        1.1683        2.1583        1.6191        1.1281        0.9075
    z=10  galaxy assembly begins                        0.4704        0.8691        0.6520        0.4542        0.3654
      (Gyr; entry = the LONGEST lifetime leaving <= eta_max surviving at that epoch)

  THE KINEMATIC WINDOW: [0.0370, 25.489] Gyr at the loosest reading, [0.0370, 0.3654] Gyr at the strictest.
  [PASS] W2  KINEMATICALLY the window is NOT empty at any of the 16 (epoch x ceiling) readings -- even the strictest ('gone by z=10' at eta <= 0.276) leaves tau_hi > tau_lo.  Task 1 alone does NOT close the escape
           (loosest [0.0370, 25.489] Gyr (ratio 689); strictest [0.0370, 0.3654] Gyr (ratio 9.9))

  PARTIAL DECAY.  If only a fraction f_dec decays and (1-f_dec) is stable, the STABLE remnant is itself a cold
  component present in galaxies today, so the SAME ceiling binds it:
      f_surv(t_0) = (1 - f_dec) + f_dec exp(-t_0/tau) <= eta_max   =>   f_dec >= 1 - eta_max, for ANY tau.
      canon eps=0   : f_dec >= 0.418  (41.8% of the CMB-required cold density destroyed)
      alt eps=0     : f_dec >= 0.514  (51.4% of the CMB-required cold density destroyed)
      canon eps=1   : f_dec >= 0.645  (64.5% of the CMB-required cold density destroyed)
      alt eps=1     : f_dec >= 0.724  (72.4% of the CMB-required cold density destroyed)
  [PASS] W3  the escape necessarily DESTROYS a large fraction of the dark matter -- at least 41.8% (canonical, eps=0) and up to 72.4% (alt, eps=1) -- for any lifetime whatsoever.  It is not a perturbative decay, which is exactly why a background cost is unavoidable
           (f_dec >= 0.418 (canon eps=0) ... 0.724 (alt eps=1), independent of tau)

======================================================================================================================
PART 2 -- TASK 2: THE BACKGROUND COST.  theta_*, BAO, SNe, age, ISW.
======================================================================================================================

  PROCEDURE.  omega_dcdm is normalised so the cold density AT RECOMBINATION equals Planck's 0.1200 -- that is
  what the third peak measures and it is the entire point of the escape.  Lambda is root-found for exact
  flatness.  r_s is recomputed with the model's own H(a).  Then (a) the theta_* shift at fixed h; (b) the h
  that restores theta_* exactly (the CMB geometric degeneracy); (c) at that h, BAO + SNe + age + an ISW proxy.

